    <bpmn:process id="W_W85" name="W85. Product Costing &amp; Margin Analysis Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly margin variance review during W9A close; or quarterly assortment review (W1); or ad-hoc triggered by significant vendor cost change (W40) or competitive pricing pressure (W61)
Frequency: Monthly margin monitoring; quarterly deep-dive review; annual category-level strategy review
Volume: 35,000 active SKUs across 200 stores + 4 DCs; ~40 product categories (13 departments per profile §6.2)
Owner: Cost Accountant
Participants: Cost Accountant, Controller, Category Managers, Pricing Analysts, VP Merchandising, CFO
Source: workflow W85 — Product Costing &amp; Margin Analysis Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W85_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W85_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W85_Lane2" name="Cost Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W85_Lane3" name="Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W85_Lane4" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W85_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W85_Start6" name="Monthly margin variance review during W9A close; or quarterly assortment review (W1); or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W85_Task7" name="System generates monthly margin analysis report per category and per SKU: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System generates monthly margin analysis report per category and per SKU: (a) gross margin % by category (current month vs. prior month vs. same month prior year vs. budget), (b) top 50 margin-declining SKUs (by margin % change month-over-month), (c) top 50 margin-improving SKUs, (d) SKUs with gross margin below minimum threshold (configurable per category, typically 15–20%), (e) WAC movement analysis — SKUs with cost change &gt; 5% in the month, (f) promo margin impact: SKUs on promotion during the month with actual vs. planned margin, (g) category-level contribution to total gross profit
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W85_Task8" name="Cost Accountant reviews margin analysis report; investigates SKUs with margin…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cost Accountant reviews margin analysis report; investigates SKUs with margin below threshold or significant margin decline: (a) cost increase not passed to SRP (W40 not executed after cost increase), (b) promotional pricing eroding margin below plan, (c) WAC distortion from small-quantity receipts at high cost, (d) vendor cost change not yet reflected in SRP decision
Responsible (R): Cost Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W85_Task9" name="Cost Accountant prepares margin exception report for Controller: top 20 margin…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Cost Accountant prepares margin exception report for Controller: top 20 margin concerns with root cause analysis and recommended action (SRP increase per W40, vendor negotiation per W44, assortment exit per W68, or accept lower margin with strategic justification)
Responsible (R): Cost Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W85_Task10" name="Controller reviews margin exception report with VP Merchandising in monthly…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Controller reviews margin exception report with VP Merchandising in monthly margin review meeting; agrees on action items with deadlines; action items tracked in system
Responsible (R): Controller / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 30 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W85_Task11" name="Cost Accountant prepares quarterly category margin deep-dive per category: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Cost Accountant prepares quarterly category margin deep-dive per category: (a) category gross margin % trend over 4 quarters, (b) category margin vs. budget and vs. target, (c) top 10 margin contributors (SKUs generating highest absolute gross profit), (d) bottom 10 margin drags (SKUs with lowest margin % and significant revenue), (e) vendor-level margin analysis — margin by vendor within each category, (f) cost structure breakdown per category: material cost, landed cost components (duty, freight, insurance), (g) import vs. domestic margin comparison, (h) promotional margin impact analysis: average margin during promo periods vs. non-promo periods
Responsible (R): Cost Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W85_Task12" name="Cost Accountant and Pricing Analyst jointly prepare pricing strategy…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Cost Accountant and Pricing Analyst jointly prepare pricing strategy recommendations per category: (a) categories where SRP increases are recommended (cost has risen but SRP not adjusted), (b) categories where competitive pricing pressure (W61 data) is limiting margin, (c) categories where vendor cost reduction should be negotiated (W44), (d) categories with structural low margin requiring assortment changes (W1, W68), (e) categories where quantity break pricing (W40.15–19) is eroding margin below acceptable levels
Responsible (R): Cost Accountant / Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W85_Task13" name="Controller and VP Merchandising review quarterly margin deep-dive together with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Controller and VP Merchandising review quarterly margin deep-dive together with Category Managers; each Category Manager presents margin improvement plan for categories below target; agreed actions integrated into W1 assortment review and W40 pricing execution
Responsible (R): Controller / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W85_Task14" name="Cost Accountant updates system margin thresholds per category if needed (based…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Cost Accountant updates system margin thresholds per category if needed (based on strategic pricing decisions); updates category margin targets for next quarter&#x27;s monitoring
Responsible (R): Cost Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W85_Task15" name="Cost Accountant prepares annual margin strategy report: (a) 12-month margin…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Cost Accountant prepares annual margin strategy report: (a) 12-month margin trend by category with quarterly granularity, (b) year-over-year margin movement by category with driver analysis (cost, mix, promo, pricing), (c) vendor rebate impact on effective margin (W27), (d) category margin vs. industry benchmarks (where available), (e) proposed margin targets by category for next year, (f) margin improvement opportunities with estimated P&amp;L impact
Responsible (R): Cost Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 16 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W85_Task16" name="CFO reviews annual margin strategy with VP Merchandising and CEO; agreed…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: CFO reviews annual margin strategy with VP Merchandising and CEO; agreed category margin targets feed into W26 annual budget as gross profit targets; significant pricing strategy changes approved and scheduled for execution through W40
Responsible (R): CFO / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W85_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W85_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W85_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W85_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-292 (ensure controlled execution — FP&amp;A &amp; Reporting (PA-17.4).) | - operational: may not handle automatically
Owner: Cost Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W85_Assoc19" sourceRef="W85_Annotation18" targetRef="W85_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow20" sourceRef="W85_Start6" targetRef="W85_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow21" sourceRef="W85_Task7" targetRef="W85_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow22" sourceRef="W85_Task8" targetRef="W85_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow23" sourceRef="W85_Task9" targetRef="W85_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow24" sourceRef="W85_Task10" targetRef="W85_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow25" sourceRef="W85_Task11" targetRef="W85_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow26" sourceRef="W85_Task12" targetRef="W85_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow27" sourceRef="W85_Task13" targetRef="W85_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow28" sourceRef="W85_Task14" targetRef="W85_Task15" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow29" sourceRef="W85_Task15" targetRef="W85_Task16" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W85_Flow30" sourceRef="W85_Task16" targetRef="W85_End17" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W85_diag">
