    <bpmn:process id="W_W1405" name="W1405. Store-Level P&amp;L Auto-Generation, Contribution Margin Analysis &amp; Monthly Financial Performance Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Month-end close cycle (W9A) — after daily POS transactions, AP accruals, and inventory adjustments are finalized for the period
Frequency: Monthly per store; 200 stores × 12 months = 2,400 P&amp;L reports/year
Volume: 200 individual store P&amp;Ls + 4 regional P&amp;L roll-ups + 1 consolidated chain P&amp;L per month
Owner: FP&amp;A Manager
Participants: FP&amp;A Analyst, Store Manager, Regional Manager, Controller, VP Store Operations, CFO
Source: workflow W1405 — Store-Level P&amp;L Auto-Generation, Contribution Margin Analysis &amp; Monthly Financial Performance Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1405_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1405_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1405_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1405_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1405_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1405_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1405_Lane2" name="FP&amp;A Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1405_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1405_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1405_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1405_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1405_Lane4" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1405_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1405_Lane5" name="FP&amp;A Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1405_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1405_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1405_Start7" name="Month-end close cycle (W9A) — after daily POS transactions, AP accruals, and inventory…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1405_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1405_Task8" name="Revenue">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System auto-generates store-level P&amp;L after month-end close is finalized (W9A completion trigger): (a) Revenue: POS sales by department (Lumber, Plumbing/Electrical, Tiles, Tools/Hardware, Paint, Appliances, Garden, Other) + ecommerce revenue allocated to ship-from-store location + trade account revenue + installation service revenue; (b) Cost of Goods Sold: WAC-based inventory cost per item sold, allocated by store; includes landed cost components (freight, duty, insurance) per SKU; (c) Gross Margin: revenue minus COGS by department and overall; (d) Direct Store Operating Expenses: store labor cost (from payroll W10 allocation), rent (to Property Mgmt Inc. per W14), utilities (electricity, water, internet), store-level maintenance and supplies (W47), store-level LP costs, depreciation of store fixtures and equipment; (e) Contribution Margin: gross margin minus direct store operating expenses; (f) Allocated Overhead: regional management cost, corporate overhead allocation (IT, HR, Finance, Marketing) allocated by revenue or selling area; (g) Store Net Income: contribution margin minus allocated overhead
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): FP&amp;A Manager
Duration: Automated (generation ~5 min per store; total ~17 hours for 200 stores — batch processed)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1405_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1405_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1405_Task9" name="System generates variance analysis: current month vs. prior month, current…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System generates variance analysis: current month vs. prior month, current month vs. same month prior year, current month vs. budget (W26), and year-to-date vs. budget; variances flagged as favorable (green) or unfavorable (red) with percentage deviation; material variances (&gt; 5% of line item or &gt; PHP 100,000) highlighted for investigation
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1405_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1405_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1405_Task10" name="FP&amp;A Analyst reviews auto-generated P&amp;Ls for anomalies: negative margins…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: FP&amp;A Analyst reviews auto-generated P&amp;Ls for anomalies: negative margins, missing cost allocations, revenue that doesn&#x27;t reconcile to POS totals (W5B), COGS that doesn&#x27;t reconcile to inventory movements (W3/W4/W18); investigates and corrects data issues with Controller support
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A Analyst
Accountable (A): FP&amp;A Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1405_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1405_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1405_Task11" name="System generates regional P&amp;L roll-ups: 5 regions (Mindanao, Visayas…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System generates regional P&amp;L roll-ups: 5 regions (Mindanao, Visayas, Luzon-outside-NCR, Metro Manila, North/Central Luzon per profile §3.1) aggregating individual store P&amp;Ls; includes inter-store comparison metrics: revenue per sqm, gross margin %, labor cost as % of revenue, contribution margin per employee
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1405_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1405_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1405_Task12" name="FP&amp;A Analyst publishes store P&amp;L packets: (a) individual store P&amp;L with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: FP&amp;A Analyst publishes store P&amp;L packets: (a) individual store P&amp;L with variance analysis sent to Store Manager and Regional Manager via ERP portal; (b) regional summary with store ranking sent to VP Store Operations; (c) chain consolidated P&amp;L with regional comparison sent to CFO and executive team
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A Analyst
Accountable (A): FP&amp;A Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1405_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1405_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1405_Task13" name="Store Manager P&amp;L review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Store Manager P&amp;L review: Store Manager reviews their store&#x27;s P&amp;L within 5 business days of publication; investigates material unfavorable variances; documents explanations for gross margin erosion (markdowns, shrinkage), labor cost overruns (overtime per W1032), or utility spikes; creates corrective action plan for top 3 unfavorable variances
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1405_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1405_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1405_Task14" name="Regional Manager store review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Regional Manager store review: Regional Manager reviews all store P&amp;Ls in their region (40–60 stores); identifies bottom 5 stores by contribution margin for targeted coaching; schedules monthly P&amp;L review calls with bottom-performing Store Managers
Responsible (R): Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1405_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1405_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1405_Task15" name="Quarterly">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Quarterly: FP&amp;A Manager prepares store P&amp;L trend analysis for CFO QBR (W231): top/bottom quartile stores by contribution margin, stores with 3+ consecutive months of negative contribution margin (flagged for potential closure evaluation), new store ramp-up performance vs. business case (W16), store-level ROI vs. chain average
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1405_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1405_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1405_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1405_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1405_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-292 (ensure controlled execution — FP&amp;A &amp; Reporting (PA-17.4).) | - operational: FP&amp;A Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: FP&amp;A Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1405_Assoc18" sourceRef="W1405_Annotation17" targetRef="W1405_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1405_Flow19" sourceRef="W1405_Start7" targetRef="W1405_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1405_Flow20" sourceRef="W1405_Task8" targetRef="W1405_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1405_Flow21" sourceRef="W1405_Task9" targetRef="W1405_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1405_Flow22" sourceRef="W1405_Task10" targetRef="W1405_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1405_Flow23" sourceRef="W1405_Task11" targetRef="W1405_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1405_Flow24" sourceRef="W1405_Task12" targetRef="W1405_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1405_Flow25" sourceRef="W1405_Task13" targetRef="W1405_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1405_Flow26" sourceRef="W1405_Task14" targetRef="W1405_Task15" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1405_Flow27" sourceRef="W1405_Task15" targetRef="W1405_End16" />
    </bpmn:process>
